{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc | sed -n '1,380p'; nl -ba test/dao/jing/file_test.cljc | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.jing.file\n     2\t  \"Content-addressed segment store backed by a private framed append-only\n     3\t   file (docs/design/dao.jing.md; dao.jing.implementation-plan.md, Decision 2\n     4\t   and invariants F1-F6).\n     5\t\n     6\t   Framing, chosen rather than inherited: each record is one frame of\n     7\t   [4-byte big-endian signed length][UTF-8 EDN text of [address payload]].\n     8\t   The length prefix is the mechanism F3 needs — it is what makes an\n     9\t   incomplete tail detectable: a tail shorter than the prefix, a negative\n    10\t   length, or a length reaching past end of file is torn and truncated to\n    11\t   the last frame boundary. EDN is the one value codec clj, cljs and cljd\n    12\t   share with structural round-trip. Integrity rests on neither choice:\n    13\t   every frame must carry a segment address that hashes to its payload\n    14\t   (B6/F4), so the day the pinned canonical byte encoding lands it replaces\n    15\t   the payload text without touching the frame — and no version header is\n    16\t   owed, because that day every minted address changes with it (dao.jing.md,\n    17\t   Canonical encoding), so re-materialization is required regardless and a\n    18\t   frame version buys nothing. No magic, no header: a file that is not a\n    19\t   content file fails per-record validation loudly.\n    20\t\n    21\t   The durable log is not a stream (Decision 2): one reader — this backend,\n    22\t   once, at open — and one writer — its own put. No cursor is handed out,\n    23\t   no descriptor projected, nothing attaches, and no dao.stream namespace is\n    24\t   required.\n    25\t\n    26\t   The handle is plain data (D1): {:put-content-fn f :get-content-fn g\n    27\t   :close-fn c} and nothing else. records (F5) is the test's view of a path:\n    28\t   every decoded frame in order, equal duplicates included.\"\n    29\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:convert\" :as convert] [\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n    30\t                       [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n    31\t            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    32\t            [dao.jing :as jing]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t;; =============================================================================\n    36\t;; Serialization / byte conversion\n    37\t;; =============================================================================\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn ->bytes\n    40\t  \"Convert a string into UTF-8 bytes on the current host.\"\n    41\t  [payload]\n    42\t  #?(:clj (.getBytes ^String payload \"UTF-8\")\n    43\t     :cljs (js/Buffer.from payload \"utf8\")\n    44\t     :cljd (typed/Uint8List.fromList (convert/utf8.encode payload))))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn bytes->str\n    48\t  \"Convert UTF-8 bytes back into a string.\"\n    49\t  [b]\n    50\t  #?(:clj (String. ^bytes b \"UTF-8\")\n    51\t     :cljs (.toString ^js b \"utf8\")\n    52\t     :cljd (convert/utf8.decode b)))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn encode-record\n    56\t  \"Encode an [address payload] pair into frame bytes (the payload text; the\n    57\t   length prefix is written by the frame layer).\"\n    58\t  [address payload]\n    59\t  (->bytes (pr-str [address payload])))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn decode-record\n    63\t  \"Decode frame bytes back into their EDN value. Returns the parsed value\n    64\t   as-is; throws on malformed EDN.\"\n    65\t  [b]\n    66\t  (edn/read-string (bytes->str b)))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t;; =============================================================================\n    70\t;; Record validation (B6 at this backend's door; F4 at replay)\n    71\t;; =============================================================================\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn- validate-address-payload!\n    74\t  [address payload]\n    75\t  (if (and (jing/segment-address? address)\n    76\t           (= (jing/segment-hash address) (jing/content-hash payload)))\n    77\t    [address payload]\n    78\t    (throw (ex-info \"Segment address does not match payload\"\n    79\t                    {:address address, :payload payload}))))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- validate-frame!\n    83\t  [record]\n    84\t  (if (and (vector? record) (= 2 (count record)))\n    85\t    (validate-address-payload! (first record) (second record))\n    86\t    (throw (ex-info \"Record is not a 2-element [address payload] vector\"\n    87\t                    {:record record}))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t;; =============================================================================\n    91\t;; Host file primitives — the only host-aware code in this namespace\n    92\t;; =============================================================================\n    93\t\n    94\t(def ^:private prefix-size 4)\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- open-file!\n    98\t  \"Open or create the file at path for reading and appending, creating\n    99\t   parent directories. Returns the host file object.\"\n   100\t  [path]\n   101\t  #?(:clj (let [f (java.io.File. path)]\n   102\t            (when-let [parent (.getParentFile f)] (.mkdirs parent))\n   103\t            (java.io.RandomAccessFile. f \"rw\"))\n   104\t     :cljs (if-not (exists? js/require)\n   105\t             (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.file requires the Node.js fs module.\"\n   106\t                             {:path path}))\n   107\t             (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")\n   108\t                   path-module (js/require \"path\")\n   109\t                   dir (.dirname path-module path)]\n   110\t               (when-not (.existsSync fs dir)\n   111\t                 (.mkdirSync fs dir #js {:recursive true}))\n   112\t               {:fs fs, :fd (.openSync fs path \"a+\")}))\n   113\t     :cljd (let [f (dart-io/File. path)\n   114\t                 dir (.-parent f)]\n   115\t             (when-not (.existsSync dir) (.createSync dir .recursive true))\n   116\t             (.openSync f .mode dart-io/FileMode.append))))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- file-length!\n   120\t  [f]\n   121\t  #?(:clj (.length ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f)\n   122\t     :cljs (.-size (.fstatSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f)))\n   123\t     :cljd (.lengthSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f)))\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(defn- read-int!\n   127\t  \"The 4-byte big-endian signed frame length at offset.\"\n   128\t  [f offset]\n   129\t  #?(:clj (do (.seek ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f offset)\n   130\t              (.readInt ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f))\n   131\t     :cljs (let [head (js/Buffer.alloc prefix-size)]\n   132\t             (.readSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f) head 0 prefix-size offset)\n   133\t             (.readInt32BE head 0))\n   134\t     :cljd (do (.setPositionSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f offset)\n   135\t               (let [^typed/Uint8List bs (.readSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f\n   136\t                                                    prefix-size)]\n   137\t                 (.getInt32 (typed/ByteData.view (.-buffer bs)) 0)))))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn- read-bytes!\n   141\t  [f offset len]\n   142\t  #?(:clj (do (.seek ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f offset)\n   143\t              (let [b (byte-array len)]\n   144\t                (.readFully ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f b)\n   145\t                b))\n   146\t     :cljs (let [buf (js/Buffer.alloc len)]\n   147\t             (.readSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f) buf 0 len offset)\n   148\t             buf)\n   149\t     :cljd (do (.setPositionSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f offset)\n   150\t               (.readSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f len))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- truncate-file!\n   154\t  [f offset]\n   155\t  #?(:clj (.setLength ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f offset)\n   156\t     :cljs (.ftruncateSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f) offset)\n   157\t     :cljd (.truncateSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f offset)))\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t(defn- append-frame!\n   161\t  \"Write the length-prefixed frame at the current end of the file.\"\n   162\t  [f frame]\n   163\t  #?(:clj (let [raf ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f\n   164\t                len (alength ^bytes frame)]\n   165\t            (.seek raf (.length raf))\n   166\t            (.writeInt raf len)\n   167\t            (.write raf ^bytes frame))\n   168\t     :cljs (let [{:keys [fs fd]} f\n   169\t                 len (.-length ^js frame)\n   170\t                 head (js/Buffer.alloc prefix-size)]\n   171\t             (.writeInt32BE head len 0)\n   172\t             (.writeSync ^js fs fd head)\n   173\t             (.writeSync ^js fs fd frame))\n   174\t     :cljd (let [raf ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f\n   175\t                 len (.-length ^typed/Uint8List frame)\n   176\t                 head (typed/ByteData. prefix-size)]\n   177\t             (.setInt32 head 0 len)\n   178\t             (.setPositionSync raf (.lengthSync raf))\n   179\t             (.writeFromSync raf (.asUint8List (.-buffer head)))\n   180\t             (.writeFromSync raf frame))))\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(defn- sync-file!\n   184\t  \"Flush the frame just written to durable storage (F1: a put is\n   185\t   acknowledged only after this).\"\n   186\t  [f]\n   187\t  #?(:clj (.sync (.getFD ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f))\n   188\t     :cljs (.fsyncSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f))\n   189\t     :cljd (.flushSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f)))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- close-file!\n   193\t  [f]\n   194\t  #?(:clj (.close ^java.io.RandomAccessFile f)\n   195\t     :cljs (.closeSync ^js (:fs f) (:fd f))\n   196\t     :cljd (.closeSync ^dart-io/RandomAccessFile f)))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t;; =============================================================================\n   200\t;; Torn-tail truncation and replay (F3, F2, F4)\n   201\t;; =============================================================================\n   202\t\n   203\t(defn- torn-tail-offset\n   204\t  \"The offset of the first incomplete frame, scanning from 0: a tail shorter\n   205\t   than the length prefix, a negative length, or a length reaching past\n   206\t   `end` is torn. Returns `end` when every frame is complete.\"\n   207\t  [f end]\n   208\t  (loop [offset 0]\n   209\t    (cond\n   210\t      (>= offset end) end\n   211\t      (< (- end offset) prefix-size) offset\n   212\t      :else (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   213\t              (if (or (neg? len) (> (+ offset prefix-size len) end))\n   214\t                offset\n   215\t                (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)))))))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn- truncate-incomplete-tail!\n   219\t  \"Truncate the incomplete tail, returning the surviving byte length.\"\n   220\t  [f]\n   221\t  (let [end (file-length! f)\n   222\t        cut (torn-tail-offset f end)]\n   223\t    (when (< cut end) (truncate-file! f cut))\n   224\t    cut))\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- replay-frames\n   228\t  \"Decode and validate every frame into the content map. An equal duplicate\n   229\t   record is tolerated (F2); an unequal record at an existing address is a\n   230\t   collision and fails the open — defensively, since B6 makes it\n   231\t   unreachable: a frame that validates hashes its payload to its address,\n   232\t   so two valid frames at one address are equal.\"\n   233\t  [f end]\n   234\t  (loop [offset 0, content {}]\n   235\t    (if (>= offset end)\n   236\t      content\n   237\t      (let [len (read-int! f offset)\n   238\t            [address payload] (validate-frame!\n   239\t                                (decode-record\n   240\t                                 (read-bytes! f (+ offset prefix-size) len)))]\n   241\t        (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)\n   242\t               (if (contains? content address)\n   243\t                 (if (= (clojure.core/get content address) payload)\n   244\t                   content\n   245\t                   (throw (ex-info\n   246\t                           \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   247\t                           {:address address})))\n   248\t                 (assoc content address payload)))))))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t;; =============================================================================\n   252\t;; Handle functions (D1, D3, F1)\n   253\t;; =============================================================================\n   254\t\n   255\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-binding]}\n   256\t\n   257\t(defn- with-lock\n   258\t  [lock f]\n   259\t  #?(:clj (locking lock (f))\n   260\t     :default (f)))\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\t(defn- make-put\n   264\t  [state f lock]\n   265\t  (fn content-put!\n   266\t    [address payload]\n   267\t    (validate-address-payload! address payload)\n   268\t    (with-lock\n   269\t      lock\n   270\t      (fn []\n   271\t        (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   272\t          (when closed?\n   273\t            (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   274\t          (if (contains? content address)\n   275\t            (if (= (clojure.core/get content address) payload)\n   276\t              :present\n   277\t              (throw (ex-info\n   278\t                       \"Collision: address already holds a different payload\"\n   279\t                       {:address address})))\n   280\t            (let [frame (encode-record address payload)]\n   281\t              (append-frame! f frame)\n   282\t              (sync-file! f)\n   283\t              (swap! state assoc-in [:content address] payload)\n   284\t              :inserted)))))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- make-get\n   288\t  [state]\n   289\t  (fn content-get\n   290\t    [address not-found]\n   291\t    (let [{:keys [closed? content]} @state]\n   292\t      (when closed?\n   293\t        (throw (ex-info \"Content file is closed\" {:address address})))\n   294\t      (clojure.core/get content address not-found))))\n   295\t\n   296\t\n   297\t(defn- make-close\n   298\t  [state f lock]\n   299\t  (fn content-close!\n   300\t    []\n   301\t    (with-lock\n   302\t      lock\n   303\t      (fn []\n   304\t        (when-not (:closed? @state)\n   305\t          (swap! state assoc :closed? true)\n   306\t          (close-file! f))\n   307\t        nil))))\n   308\t\n   309\t\n   310\t;; =============================================================================\n   311\t;; Constructor\n   312\t;; =============================================================================\n   313\t\n   314\t(defn create-content-file\n   315\t  \"Open or create a content file at path: truncate any incomplete tail\n   316\t   (F3), replay every record into an in-memory content map (F2, F4), and\n   317\t   return the plain-data handle {:put-content-fn :get-content-fn\n   318\t   :close-fn} (D1). A record that cannot be decoded, is not a two-element\n   319\t   [address payload] vector, carries a non-segment address, or does not\n   320\t   hash to its payload fails the open, loudly (F4).\"\n   321\t  [path]\n   322\t  (let [f (open-file! path)]\n   323\t    (try (let [recovered (replay-frames f (truncate-incomplete-tail! f))\n   324\t               state (atom {:closed? false, :content recovered})\n   325\t               lock #?(:clj (Object.)\n   326\t                       :cljs (js-obj)\n   327\t                       :cljd (Object.))]\n   328\t           {:put-content-fn (make-put state f lock),\n   329\t            :get-content-fn (make-get state),\n   330\t            :close-fn (make-close state f lock)})\n   331\t         (catch #?(:clj Exception\n   332\t                   :cljs :default\n   333\t                   :cljd Object)\n   334\t                e\n   335\t           (try (close-file! f)\n   336\t                (catch #?(:clj Exception\n   337\t                          :cljs :default\n   338\t                          :cljd Object)\n   339\t                       _\n   340\t                  nil))\n   341\t           (throw e)))))\n   342\t\n   343\t\n   344\t;; =============================================================================\n   345\t;; The test's view of a path (F5)\n   346\t;; =============================================================================\n   347\t\n   348\t(defn records\n   349\t  \"The decoded, validated record vector of the file at path — every frame\n   350\t   in order, equal duplicates included. Opens with tail truncation, reads\n   351\t   and closes. This is the file backend's test-facing view (D4): what the\n   352\t   in-memory map holds is observable through the handle; what the file\n   353\t   holds is observable here.\"\n   354\t  [path]\n   355\t  (let [f (open-file! path)]\n   356\t    (try (let [end (truncate-incomplete-tail! f)]\n   357\t           (loop [offset 0, acc []]\n   358\t             (if (>= offset end)\n   359\t               acc\n   360\t               (let [len (read-int! f offset)]\n   361\t                 (recur (+ offset prefix-size len)\n   362\t                        (conj acc (validate-frame!\n   363\t                                    (decode-record\n   364\t                                     (read-bytes! f (+ offset prefix-size)\n   365\t                                                  len)))))))))\n   366\t         (finally (close-file! f)))))\n     1\t(ns dao.jing.file-test\n     2\t  \"The file backend, written from the plan's invariants F1-F6 and D1-D5\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md, P1) — not ported from the\n     4\t   v1 tests. records is the file-side view (D4/F5); the handle view is\n     5\t   materialize!/get through :put-content-fn/:get-content-fn (D1). No\n     6\t   observer or pool appears here: the pool drains in file_test are P2's.\"\n     7\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io] [\"dart:typed_data\" :as typed]])\n     8\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     9\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    10\t            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]))\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t;; =============================================================================\n    14\t;; Host helpers — raw bytes into the file, per host, for torn tails and\n    15\t;; hand-written frames. These are the only host-aware lines in the suite.\n    16\t;; =============================================================================\n    17\t\n    18\t(defn- temp-path\n    19\t  [prefix]\n    20\t  (str \"target/test-jing-content-\" prefix \"-\" (random-uuid) \".log\"))\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn- cleanup-file\n    24\t  [path]\n    25\t  #?(:clj (let [f (java.io.File. path)] (when (.exists f) (.delete f)))\n    26\t     :cljs (try (.unlinkSync (js/require \"fs\") path) (catch :default _))\n    27\t     :cljd (try (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n    28\t                  (when (.existsSync f) (.deleteSync f)))\n    29\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object\n    30\t                          :default Exception)\n    31\t                       _\n    32\t                  nil))))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- host-bytes\n    36\t  \"A host byte object from a seq of ints 0-255.\"\n    37\t  [ints]\n    38\t  #?(:clj (byte-array (mapv unchecked-byte ints))\n    39\t     :cljs (js/Buffer.from (clj->js (vec ints)))\n    40\t     :cljd (typed/Uint8List.fromList ints)))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn- int32-be\n    44\t  \"The four bytes of n as a big-endian signed int32.\"\n    45\t  [n]\n    46\t  (mapv #(bit-and (bit-shift-right n %) 0xFF) [24 16 8 0]))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- byte-count\n    50\t  [bs]\n    51\t  #?(:clj (alength bs) :cljs (.-length bs) :cljd (.-length bs)))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- bytes->ints\n    55\t  [bs]\n    56\t  #?(:clj (mapv #(bit-and (int %) 0xFF) bs)\n    57\t     :cljs (vec (js/Array.from bs))\n    58\t     :cljd (vec bs)))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- frame-of\n    62\t  \"A complete frame around record bytes: the big-endian length prefix the\n    63\t   backend writes, then the bytes. encode-record produces record bytes only\n    64\t   — the prefix is the frame layer's, so a raw append must go through here\n    65\t   to produce what the scanner treats as a frame rather than a torn tail.\"\n    66\t  [record-bytes]\n    67\t  (host-bytes (concat (int32-be (byte-count record-bytes))\n    68\t                      (bytes->ints record-bytes))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- append-raw-bytes!\n    72\t  \"Append raw host bytes at the end of the file at path, bypassing the\n    73\t   backend — the torn-tail and fail-closed cases must reach the framing\n    74\t   layer from outside it. Takes a byte object: encode-record output, or\n    75\t   (host-bytes (int32-be n)) composed with payload ints.\"\n    76\t  [path bs]\n    77\t  #?(:clj (with-open [raf (java.io.RandomAccessFile.\n    78\t                           (java.io.File. path) \"rw\")]\n    79\t            (.seek raf (.length raf))\n    80\t            (.write raf bs))\n    81\t     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")\n    82\t                 fd (.openSync fs path \"a\")]\n    83\t             (try (.writeSync fs fd bs)\n    84\t                  (finally (.closeSync fs fd))))\n    85\t     :cljd (let [raf (.openSync (dart-io/File. path)\n    86\t                                .mode dart-io/FileMode.append)]\n    87\t             (try (.writeFromSync raf bs)\n    88\t                  (finally (.closeSync raf))))))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t;; =============================================================================\n    92\t;; F1, F2, B5, B7 — storage and retrieval\n    93\t;; =============================================================================\n    94\t\n    95\t(deftest round-trip-of-every-payload-kind\n    96\t  (testing\n    97\t    \"F1/F2/B5: materialize! derives the address, the backend stores exactly\n    98\t            the payload, and every payload kind round-trips — including nil,\n    99\t            distinct from absence, and the keyword that was once a sentinel\"\n   100\t    (let [path (temp-path \"roundtrip\")\n   101\t          ;; B7: keyword payloads, the former sentinel value among them, so\n   102\t          ;; a regression to a keyword not-found sentinel is caught here.\n   103\t          payloads [nil\n   104\t                    \"plain text\"\n   105\t                    :dao.jing/content-missing\n   106\t                    42\n   107\t                    -7\n   108\t                    true\n   109\t                    [1 2 3]\n   110\t                    {:a 1, :b {:nested [true nil \"s\"]}}\n   111\t                    #{:x :y}]\n   112\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   113\t      (try\n   114\t        (doseq [payload payloads]\n   115\t          (let [address (jing/materialize! handle payload)]\n   116\t            (is (jing/segment-address? address))\n   117\t            (is (= payload (jing/get handle address ::absent))\n   118\t                (str \"round trip of \" (pr-str payload)))\n   119\t            ;; B5: a stored nil is nil, not the not-found sentinel.\n   120\t            (when (nil? payload)\n   121\t              (is (nil? (jing/get handle address ::absent))))))\n   122\t        (is (= ::absent\n   123\t               (jing/get handle (jing/segment-key {:never \"written\"})\n   124\t                        ::absent))\n   125\t            \"an absent address returns only the caller's sentinel\")\n   126\t        (finally (jing/close! handle) (cleanup-file path))))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t(deftest put-verdicts-and-records-are-the-file\n   130\t  (testing\n   131\t    \"F1/F5: the first put is acknowledged :inserted after its flush, an\n   132\t            equal put is :present and writes no record, and records is the\n   133\t            file itself — every frame, in order\"\n   134\t    (let [path (temp-path \"verdicts\")\n   135\t          a1 (jing/segment-key \"one\")\n   136\t          a2 (jing/segment-key {:two 2})\n   137\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   138\t      (try\n   139\t        (is (= :inserted ((:put-content-fn handle) a1 \"one\")))\n   140\t        (is (= :present ((:put-content-fn handle) a1 \"one\")))\n   141\t        (is (= 1 (count (jing-file/records path)))\n   142\t            \"an equal put writes no record\")\n   143\t        (is (= :inserted ((:put-content-fn handle) a2 {:two 2})))\n   144\t        (is (= [[a1 \"one\"] [a2 {:two 2}]] (jing-file/records path))\n   145\t            \"records preserves frame order, duplicates included\")\n   146\t        (finally (jing/close! handle) (cleanup-file path))))))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(deftest invalid-put-writes-nothing\n   150\t  (testing\n   151\t    \"B6: the backend validates at its own door — a non-segment address or an\n   152\t            address that does not hash to the payload throws and stores\n   153\t            nothing\"\n   154\t    (let [path (temp-path \"invalid-put\")\n   155\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   156\t      (try\n   157\t        (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   158\t                     ((:put-content-fn handle) :root/not-content \"x\")))\n   159\t        (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   160\t                     ((:put-content-fn handle) (jing/segment-key \"y\") \"x\")))\n   161\t        (is (= [] (jing-file/records path)) \"nothing was written\")\n   162\t        (finally (jing/close! handle) (cleanup-file path))))))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t;; =============================================================================\n   166\t;; F2, F4 — replay, duplicates, and failing the open\n   167\t;; =============================================================================\n   168\t\n   169\t(deftest durability-across-close-and-reopen\n   170\t  (testing\n   171\t    \"F2/F5: every record replays into the content map on the next open\"\n   172\t    (let [path (temp-path \"durability\")\n   173\t          a1 (jing/segment-key \"alpha\")\n   174\t          a2 (jing/segment-key {:n 2})\n   175\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   176\t      (jing/materialize! handle \"alpha\")\n   177\t      (jing/materialize! handle {:n 2})\n   178\t      (jing/close! handle)\n   179\t      (let [h2 (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   180\t        (try (is (= \"alpha\" (jing/get h2 a1 ::absent)))\n   181\t             (is (= {:n 2} (jing/get h2 a2 ::absent)))\n   182\t             (finally (jing/close! h2) (cleanup-file path)))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(deftest acknowledged-insert-survives-immediate-close\n   186\t  (testing\n   187\t    \"F1/F5: the :inserted verdict is returned only after the flush, so an\n   188\t            immediate close cannot lose the record\"\n   189\t    (let [path (temp-path \"ack\")\n   190\t          payload {:ack 1}\n   191\t          address (jing/segment-key payload)\n   192\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   193\t      (jing/materialize! handle payload)\n   194\t      (jing/close! handle)\n   195\t      (let [h2 (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   196\t        (try (is (= payload (jing/get h2 address ::absent)))\n   197\t             (finally (jing/close! h2) (cleanup-file path)))))))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(deftest equal-duplicate-frames-recover\n   201\t  (testing\n   202\t    \"F2: an equal duplicate record is tolerated on replay; the duplicate\n   203\t            frame is visible to records and writes nothing new\"\n   204\t    (let [path (temp-path \"dup\")\n   205\t          address (jing/segment-key {:k 1})\n   206\t          payload {:k 1}\n   207\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   208\t      (jing/materialize! handle payload)\n   209\t      (jing/close! handle)\n   210\t      ;; Hand-write the identical frame again, bypassing the backend.\n   211\t      (append-raw-bytes! path (frame-of (jing-file/encode-record address payload)))\n   212\t      (is (= 2 (count (jing-file/records path)))\n   213\t          \"records sees both frames, equal duplicates included\")\n   214\t      (let [h2 (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   215\t        (try (is (= payload (jing/get h2 address ::absent)))\n   216\t             (is (= :present ((:put-content-fn h2) address payload)))\n   217\t             (is (= 2 (count (jing-file/records path)))\n   218\t                 \"a :present put writes no record\")\n   219\t             (finally (jing/close! h2) (cleanup-file path)))))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(deftest fail-closed-categories-fail-the-open\n   223\t  (testing\n   224\t    \"F4: a complete frame that cannot be decoded, is not a two-element\n   225\t            vector, carries a non-segment address, or does not hash to its\n   226\t            payload fails the open, loudly\"\n   227\t    (let [good (jing/segment-key \"ok\")]\n   228\t      (doseq [[name frame-bytes]\n   229\t              [[\"malformed EDN\" (frame-of (jing-file/->bytes \"[[[not edn\"))]\n   230\t               [\"wrong shape\"\n   231\t                (frame-of (jing-file/->bytes (pr-str [good \"ok\" :extra])))]\n   232\t               [\"invalid address\"\n   233\t                (frame-of (jing-file/->bytes (pr-str [:root/not-content \"ok\"])))]\n   234\t               [\"hash mismatch\"\n   235\t                (frame-of (jing-file/->bytes (pr-str [good \"different\"])))]]]\n   236\t        (let [path (temp-path \"corrupt\")]\n   237\t          (append-raw-bytes! path frame-bytes)\n   238\t          (try (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   239\t                            (jing-file/create-content-file path))\n   240\t                   name)\n   241\t               (finally (cleanup-file path))))))))\n   242\t\n   243\t\n   244\t(deftest unequal-duplicate-at-one-address-fails-the-open\n   245\t  (testing\n   246\t    \"F2's collision case. Two individually valid frames at one address must\n   247\t            be equal (B6: the address hashes the payload), so an unequal\n   248\t            duplicate necessarily fails the second frame's own hash check —\n   249\t            the open fails on F4's ground before the accumulation's\n   250\t            defensive collision branch, which is unreachable by\n   251\t            construction, is ever reached\"\n   252\t    (let [path (temp-path \"collision\")\n   253\t          good (jing/segment-key \"ok\")]\n   254\t      (append-raw-bytes! path (frame-of (jing-file/encode-record good \"ok\")))\n   255\t      (append-raw-bytes!\n   256\t        path (frame-of (jing-file/->bytes (pr-str [good \"other\"]))))\n   257\t      (try (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   258\t                        (jing-file/create-content-file path)))\n   259\t           (finally (cleanup-file path))))))\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\t;; =============================================================================\n   263\t;; F3 — torn-tail truncation, each category hand-written per host\n   264\t;; =============================================================================\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- torn-tail-recovers\n   267\t  \"The F3 proof shape: one valid record, a torn tail of raw bytes, and the\n   268\t   open must truncate, replay the survivor, accept a clean put, and reopen\n   269\t   with both records.\"\n   270\t  [prefix torn-bytes]\n   271\t  (let [path (temp-path prefix)\n   272\t        a1 (jing/segment-key \"survivor\")\n   273\t        a2 (jing/segment-key {:after :truncation})\n   274\t        handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   275\t    (jing/materialize! handle \"survivor\")\n   276\t    (jing/close! handle)\n   277\t    (append-raw-bytes! path torn-bytes)\n   278\t    (try\n   279\t      (let [h2 (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   280\t        ;; close is idempotent, so the outer finally may re-close h2.\n   281\t        (try\n   282\t          (is (= [[a1 \"survivor\"]] (jing-file/records path))\n   283\t              \"the torn tail is truncated; only the survivor replays\")\n   284\t          (is (= \"survivor\" (jing/get h2 a1 ::absent)))\n   285\t          (jing/materialize! h2 {:after :truncation})\n   286\t          (jing/close! h2)\n   287\t          (let [h3 (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   288\t            (try\n   289\t              (is (= [[a1 \"survivor\"] [a2 {:after :truncation}]]\n   290\t                     (jing-file/records path))\n   291\t                  \"a put after truncation lands clean and survives\")\n   292\t              (is (= {:after :truncation} (jing/get h3 a2 ::absent)))\n   293\t              (finally (jing/close! h3))))\n   294\t          (finally (jing/close! h2))))\n   295\t      (finally (cleanup-file path)))))\n   296\t\n   297\t\n   298\t(deftest torn-tail-overlong-length-is-truncated\n   299\t  (testing\n   300\t    \"F3: a length reaching past end of file is torn — int32 999 with only\n   301\t            two payload bytes (hand-written, not the v1 fixture: the torn\n   302\t            bytes must follow a valid record)\"\n   303\t    (torn-tail-recovers \"torn-overlong\"\n   304\t                        (host-bytes (into (int32-be 999) [1 2])))))\n   305\t\n   306\t\n   307\t(deftest torn-tail-shorter-than-prefix-is-truncated\n   308\t  (testing \"F3: a tail shorter than the 4-byte length prefix is torn\"\n   309\t    (torn-tail-recovers \"torn-subprefix\" (host-bytes [7 7]))))\n   310\t\n   311\t\n   312\t(deftest torn-tail-negative-length-is-truncated\n   313\t  (testing \"F3: a negative frame length is torn\"\n   314\t    (torn-tail-recovers \"torn-negative\" (host-bytes (int32-be -1)))))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t;; =============================================================================\n   318\t;; D2, D3, F6 — handle lifecycle\n   319\t;; =============================================================================\n   320\t\n   321\t(deftest close-semantics\n   322\t  (testing\n   323\t    \"D2/D3/F6: close! returns nil and is idempotent; after close every\n   324\t            entry point throws; stored content is neither cleared nor\n   325\t            rewritten\"\n   326\t    (let [path (temp-path \"close\")\n   327\t          payload {:v 1}\n   328\t          address (jing/segment-key payload)\n   329\t          handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   330\t      (jing/materialize! handle payload)\n   331\t      (is (nil? (jing/close! handle)))\n   332\t      (is (nil? (jing/close! handle)) \"close is idempotent\")\n   333\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   334\t                   (jing/materialize! handle {:x 1})))\n   335\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   336\t                   (jing/get handle address ::absent)))\n   337\t      (is (thrown? #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default :cljd Object)\n   338\t                   ((:put-content-fn handle) address payload)))\n   339\t      (is (= [[address payload]] (jing-file/records path))\n   340\t          \"closing does not clear or rewrite the file\")\n   341\t      (cleanup-file path))))\n   342\t\n   343\t\n   344\t(deftest contention-writes-exactly-one-record\n   345\t  (testing\n   346\t    \"D5/F6: under JVM contention, N concurrent puts of one payload yield\n   347\t            exactly one :inserted, N-1 :present, and one record\"\n   348\t    #?(:clj (let [path (temp-path \"contention\")\n   349\t                  payload {:contended true}\n   350\t                  address (jing/segment-key payload)\n   351\t                  handle (jing-file/create-content-file path)]\n   352\t              (try (let [results (mapv #(deref % 5000 ::timeout)\n   353\t                                       (doall (repeatedly\n   354\t                                                16\n   355\t                                                (fn []\n   356\t                                                  (future\n   357\t                                                    ((:put-content-fn handle)\n   358\t                                                     address payload))))))]\n   359\t                     (is (not-any? #{::timeout} results))\n   360\t                     (is (= 1 (count (filter #{:inserted} results))))\n   361\t                     (is (= 15 (count (filter #{:present} results))))\n   362\t                     (is (= [[address payload]] (jing-file/records path))))\n   363\t                   (finally (jing/close! handle) (cleanup-file path))))\n   364\t       :cljs (is true \"JVM contention is a clj-only property\")\n   365\t       :cljd (is true \"JVM contention is a clj-only property\"))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
