{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"grep -n -A8 -B2 'F2\\\\|Deletion\\\\|delete\\\\|cljd-out\\\\|generated Dart' docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md | head -120\"","aggregated_output":"5-[`dao.jing.md`](./dao.jing.md) (the design). `dao.stream` is implemented\n6-and stable on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd. This document says how to **build\n7:`dao.jing` on it and delete what is there**. The existing implementation and\n8-its tests have no authority; two things do: the contract, and the invariants\n9-listed below. Revisions 1–6 are the record of how those invariants were\n10-argued out (`cdb871c` is revision 5). Revision 8 introduced a shared\n11-observation step; this revision corrects where that step comes from. This\n12-document is transient.\n13-\n14-## What DaoJing is, in one paragraph\n15-\n--\n184-- F1 [D] Each record is `[address payload]` appended to a file; a put is\n185-  acknowledged `:inserted` only after the write is flushed.\n186:- F2 [D] On open, the file is replayed into the content map. An equal\n187-  duplicate record is tolerated; an unequal record at an existing address\n188-  is a collision and the open fails.\n189-- F3 [D] An incomplete tail is truncated before replay — shorter than the\n190-  length prefix, a negative length, a length past end of file. After\n191-  truncation the surviving records replay and a subsequent put lands clean.\n192-  Correctness evidence for the truncation code; there is no stored content\n193-  to be compatible with, and the framing is free.\n194-- F4 [D] A complete record that cannot be decoded, is not a two-element\n--\n543-## What is built, in four phases\n544-\n545:Each phase builds something checkable on clj, cljs (Node) and cljd, deletes\n546-what it replaces, and leaves the suite green. Order is by dependency: the\n547-core first, because three callers go through it and two of them ship today;\n548-the file backend depends only on B and D; the pool depends on the core and on\n549-both ends of the pool being v2; the prose depends on all three being real.\n550-\n551-### P0 — The core step, and its two shipped callers\n552-\n553-**Build** `src/cljc/dao/stream/observe.cljc` per Decision 0: `step`,\n--\n670-| phase | clj | cljs (Node) | cljd | notes                                                                                                      |\n671-| ----- | --- | ----------- | ---- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n672:| P0    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | pure `.cljc`; `forward`, VM, serving, ws and REPL suites unchanged; cljd lane regenerates `test/cljd-out/` |\n673-| P1    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | three host branches in `dao.jing.file`; torn-tail bytes hand-written per host                              |\n674-| P2    | ✓   | ✓           | ✓    | pure `.cljc`                                                                                               |\n675-| P3    | —   | —           | —    | prose                                                                                                      |\n676-\n677-## Invariants of the whole, checked\n678-\n679-No hidden global state: `dao.stream.observe` and `dao.jing` hold no atom;\n680-backend state is per-handle; P1 removes a `defopen` from the ambient\n--\n689-## Boundary\n690-\n691:**Built or deleted here:** `dao.stream.observe` (new), the loop bodies of\n692-`dao.stream.forward` and `yin.vm.stream-observer` (exports unchanged),\n693-`dao.jing`, `dao.jing.file`, `dao.jing.mem` (kept), `dao.stream.log`\n694:(deleted), the two writer seams in `dao.space.index` and\n695-`dao.space.transactor`, `observe_test` (new), `jing_test`, `mem_test`,\n696:`file_test`, `log_test` (deleted), the pool cases in `dht_test` and the five\n697-`dao.space` tests, one comment in `btree_durability_test`, `dao.jing.md`.\n698-\n699-**Not here, each with its home:** `dao.jing.remote`, `remote_test` and\n700-`dao.jing.coordinate`'s remote branch — Decision 3, `dao.space`'s plan;\n701-`dao.jing.dht*` — the UDP transport, deferred by the stream plan; everything\n702-else in `dao.space*` — its own plan; the content write path as an effect\n703-stream — a DaoJing architecture item; a content-serving endpoint — whatever\n704-product surface needs it; canonical encoding, durable checkpoints and a\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
